# Standing-projection gate (event-sourced standing law): derives each
# WorkOrder's CURRENT standing from its append-only StandingTransition chain.
# A chain tip is an event whose toStanding is not any other event's
# fromStanding for the same work order; the tip's toStanding IS the
# projection. WorkOrders with no transitions return no row here — their
# projection is the declared sj:standing (consumers default to it; the
# kernel equivalent is GgenIgniter.SemanticJira.project_standing/1 over the
# transition log with declared-standing fallback at the call site).
# A forked chain (two competing tips, e.g. two events from one standing)
# returns BOTH tips: the jira template refuses on more than one distinct
# projected standing per work order, so ambiguity fails closed instead of
# silently picking a branch. Guarded by GgenIgniter.SemanticJiraPackTest
# "every pack gate executes" and the event-sourcing suite's kernel-vs-SPARQL
# equivalence proof.
PREFIX sj: <https://ggen-igniter.dev/ontology/semantic-jira#>
PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
SELECT ?work_order ?id ?declared ?projected WHERE {
  ?work_order a sj:WorkOrder ;
              dcterms:identifier ?id ;
              sj:standing ?declared .
  ?tip a sj:StandingTransition ;
       sj:transitionWorkOrder ?work_order ;
       sj:toStanding ?projected .
  MINUS {
    ?follower a sj:StandingTransition ;
              sj:transitionWorkOrder ?work_order ;
              sj:fromStanding ?projected .
  }
}
ORDER BY ?id ?projected
